    "media:imagetext": "the\nlifejacket fully\ninflated\nORAL INFLATION\nTUBE \u0026 VALVE\nINFLATOR\nSEA LIGHT\nWHISTLE\nTIE TAPES\nWATER ACTIVATED\nCELLI\n\"JERK TO INFLATE\"\nTAG\nGAS CYLINDER\nRED\nRemove jacket from valise\nPass over head\nTie tapes around waist\nInflate by pulling Red toggle\nRe-inflate or top-up using\nThe light will luminate when\nmouth-piece (this may be one\njacket comes into contact with\nof two types).\nwater except when a tab is\nTo increase pressure, blow\nprovided, in this case pull cord\nthrough the mouth valve In\nwill completely detached\nthe Type A shown right, pres\nA\nsure is reduced by depressing\nthe spigot in the valve mouth.\nIn the Type B the special\ntongue on the cap is inserted\ninto the valve mouth to\ndepress the valve.\nRFD TYPE 102 LIFEJACKETS FOR OLDER\nCHILDREN C.A.A. APPROVED\nOlder children use the TYPE 102, but the tie-tapes\nshould be secured around the body and over the\nbuoyancy chamber.\nin an\nEMERGENCY\nOn receiving emergency warning, loosen\nclothing at the neck and remove shoes.\nYour life jacket is stowed close to hand.\nDo not inflate life jacket until after leaving\naircraft or instructed by a crew member.\nThe mouth tube is ONLY for topping-up\npressure DO NOT orally inflate life jacket\nprior to pulling inflation tag.",
